10
00:42:51,428 --> 00:42:57,428
Zombie apocalypse is a subgenre of apocalyptic and post-apocalyptic fiction in
which society collapses due to overwhelming swarms of zombies.

11
00:47:08,571 --> 00:47:14,571
Usually, only a few individuals or small bands of
human survivors are left living.

12
00:51:25,714 --> 00:51:31,714
There are many different causes of a zombie apocalypse in fiction.

13
00:55:42,857 --> 00:55:48,857
In some versions, the reason the dead rise and attack humans is unknown; in others, a
parasite or infection is the cause - framing the film like a plague.

14
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
Some stories have every corpse zombify regardless of the cause of death, whereas others
require exposure to the infection, most commonly in the form of a bite.

15
01:04:17,142 --> 01:04:23,142
The genre originated in the 1968 American horror film Night of
the Living Dead, which was directed by George A.

16
01:08:34,285 --> 01:08:40,285
Romero, who took inspiration from the 1954 novel
I Am Legend by Richard Matheson.

17
01:12:51,428 --> 01:12:57,428
Romero's film introduced the concept of the flesh-eating zombie and spawned numerous
other fictional works, including films, video games, and literature.

18
01:17:08,571 --> 01:17:14,571
The zombie apocalypse has been used as a metaphor for various contemporary fears, such
as global contagion, the breakdown of society, and the end of the world.

19
01:21:25,714 --> 01:21:31,714
It has repeatedly been referenced in the media and has inspired various fan activities such as
zombie walks, making zombie apocalypse a dominant genre in popular culture.

20
01:25:42,857 --> 01:25:48,857
The tone is dark and thought_provoking.
